          "text": "# State Management in AG-UI\n\nAG-UI provides a sophisticated state synchronization system for real-time coordination between AI agents and frontend applications.\n\n## Core Architecture\n\nThe system operates on a shared state model where data persists across interactions and both parties can access and modify it. This creates a \"bidirectional communication channel\" enabling agents to make contextual decisions while frontends observe backend changes.\n\n## Synchronization Methods\n\nTwo complementary approaches handle state updates:\n\n**State Snapshots** deliver complete state representations, typically during initialization, after interruptions, or when major changes occur. Upon receipt, frontends should \"replace its existing state model entirely.\"\n\n**State Deltas** use JSON Patch format (RFC 6902) to send incremental changes, proving more bandwidth-efficient for frequent small updates or large objects where most properties remain static.\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nThe AG-UI implementation applies patches using the `fast-json-patch` library with atomic operations that don't mutate the original state. If inconsistencies arise after applying patches, frontends can request a fresh snapshot.\n\n## Real-World Application\n\nCopilotKit exemplifies this approach through hooks like `useCoAgent()`, enabling frontends to read and update agent state in real-time, while backend agents emit updates via `copilotkit_emit_state()`.\n\n## Key Recommendations\n\nBest practices emphasize judicious snapshot usage, preferring deltas for incremental changes, thoughtful state structuring, conflict resolution strategies, error recovery mechanisms, and security considerations regarding sensitive data.",
