          "type": "user",
          "text": "# Events in the Agent User Interaction Protocol\n\nThe Agent User Interaction Protocol employs \"a streaming event-based architecture\" where events function as fundamental communication units between agents and frontends.\n\n## Event Categories\n\nSeven main event categories exist:\n\n- **Lifecycle Events**: Track agent run progression\n- **Text Message Events**: Handle streaming textual content\n- **Tool Call Events**: Manage tool executions\n- **State Management Events**: Synchronize agent-UI state\n- **Activity Events**: Represent ongoing progress\n- **Special Events**: Support custom functionality\n- **Draft Events**: Proposed developments under review\n\n## Core Structure\n\nAll events share three base properties: `type` (event identifier), `timestamp` (optional creation time), and `rawEvent` (optional original data).\n\n## Key Patterns\n\nThe protocol implements three primary interaction patterns:\n\n1. **Start-Content-End**: Streams content incrementally (text, tool arguments)\n2. **Snapshot-Delta**: Synchronizes state efficiently using complete snapshots followed by JSON Patch updates\n3. **Lifecycle**: Monitors agent runs with mandatory start/end events and optional step tracking\n\n## Notable Event Types\n\n**Lifecycle**: RunStarted (mandatory beginning), RunFinished/RunError (mandatory endings), plus optional StepStarted/StepFinished for progress tracking\n\n**Streaming**: TextMessageStart/Content/End for messages; ToolCallStart/Args/End for tool invocations\n\n**State**: StateSnapshot (complete state), StateDelta (incremental RFC 6902 patches), MessagesSnapshot (conversation history)\n\n**Extensions**: Raw events (external system passthrough), Custom events (application-specific), and draft Reasoning/Meta events under development",
