          "text": "# AG-UI Messages Documentation Summary\n\nThe AG-UI Messages documentation outlines a vendor-neutral communication protocol for conversational AI systems. Here are the key points:\n\n## Core Concept\nMessages form \"the backbone of communication in the AG-UI protocol,\" representing conversation history between users and AI agents while maintaining compatibility across different AI providers like OpenAI and Anthropic.\n\n## Message Types Supported\nThe system defines six message roles:\n- **User Messages**: Support both plain text and multimodal content (images, audio, files)\n- **Assistant Messages**: Can include optional text and tool calls\n- **System Messages**: Provide instructions or context\n- **Tool Messages**: Contain execution results linked to specific tool calls\n- **Activity Messages**: Structured progress updates rendered by frontends\n- **Developer Messages**: Internal debugging communication\n\n## Key Features\n\n**Streaming Architecture**: Messages support three-phase streaming (start, content chunks, end) for real-time responsiveness. Tool calls similarly stream in phases to show agent reasoning progressively.\n\n**Tool Integration**: Tool calls are embedded in assistant messages, with results returned via tool messages that reference the original call ID, creating a traceable chain of actions.\n\n**Synchronization**: Two mechanisms handle message sync—complete snapshots for initialization and major state changes, plus streaming for ongoing interactions.\n\nThe documentation emphasizes that this standardized structure enables \"sophisticated conversational AI experiences\" while preserving flexibility across different backend services.",
