          "text": "# AG-UI Server Implementation Guide\n\nThis documentation explains how to build an AG-UI-compatible HTTP server that streams responses from OpenAI's GPT-4o model.\n\n## Key Concepts\n\nThe guide describes server implementations as ideal when \"you're building a new agent from scratch or want a dedicated service for your agent capabilities.\" Developers gain maximum control over event emission and can expose agents as standalone APIs.\n\n## Architecture Overview\n\nThe implementation involves:\n\n1. **Setup Phase** – Initialize the OpenAI client and emit a `RUN_STARTED` event\n2. **Request Processing** – Send user messages to the chat completions endpoint with streaming enabled\n3. **Response Streaming** – Forward each data chunk as either `TEXT_MESSAGE_CHUNK` or `TOOL_CALL_CHUNK` events\n4. **Completion** – Emit `RUN_FINISHED` or `RUN_ERROR` events\n\n## Technical Requirements\n\nPrerequisites include Python 3.12+, Poetry, and an OpenAI API key. The setup process involves cloning the AG-UI repository, copying the server-starter template, and updating package metadata and class definitions.\n\n## Event Flow\n\nThe server follows a structured event sequence: lifecycle events signal the run's beginning, middle, and end, while content events stream the actual message fragments and tool invocations back to the client in real-time.\n\n## Community Contributions\n\nThe documentation welcomes custom server implementations through pull requests to the AG-UI repository, encouraging developers to share reusable integrations with the broader ecosystem.",
